{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_36puqkgig55r57efrhs25ppmgejseeqrkixktio24v5ibu7e4vbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nThe Rust translation is verified byte-identical to the C implementation.\n\n**Configuration analysis:**\n- `Cargo.toml` defines NO `[features]` section, so there is exactly **one** valid feature combination — the default. `cargo check --no-default-features` succeeds.\n- `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no conditional configuration (just `add_executable(driver src/main.c src/lib.c)`).\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Added `[lib]` with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]` to `Cargo.toml` so Rust produces an exported `.so`. Added `libloading = \"0.8\"` as a dev-dependency.\n2. Created `src/lib.rs` with a `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn process_buffer(...)` shim matching the C ABI exactly. Updated `src/main.rs` to import via the new lib crate.\n3. Built the C source as a shared library at `/tmp/harvest-work-DdMYpi/c_build/libdriver_c.so` (without modifying anything in `c_src/`).\n4. Wrote `tests/ffi_compare.rs` with 16 integration tests that load **both** `.so` files via `libloading` and call `process_buffer` through the FFI symbol — never calling Rust functions directly. Tests cover empty buffers, no-op flags, rotate (small + large offset paths, negative offsets, oversized offsets), compact runs (with run-length-cap-at-255 path), remove duplicates (both order modes), interleave halves, reverse segments, all 32 flag combinations × multiple parameters, and 200 pseudorandom inputs.\n5. The tests use a `2048`-byte backing buffer because the C `compact_runs` (with small thresholds) transiently writes past `length` — both impls need the same overprovisioned memory to be byte-identical. The Rust FFI shim creates a slice of `length*2 + 64` to permit the same access pattern.\n6. **All 16 tests pass in both `cargo test` and `cargo test --release`.**\n7. `nm -D` comparison: both `.so` files export the same functional symbol (`process_buffer`); other symbols in the C `.so` (`__bss_start`, `_edata`, `_end`, `_init`, `_fini`) are linker-generated ELF metadata, not API surface."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":52005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":293,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7789b5a-1796-4b79-88f2-3400c1f0f704","uuid":"26a353ff-e14f-45e0-8818-d5112ab507a4"}
